From: Xiang Mei <xmei5@asu.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] media: usbtv: only scan chunk positions that hold a whole chunk

usbtv_iso_cb() walks every isochronous packet in USBTV_CHUNK_SIZE (256 byte)
steps and bounds only the chunk *start* against the packet's actual_length.
An accepted chunk, however, consumes a 4-byte header word plus USBTV_CHUNK
(240) image words - 964 bytes - because usbtv_chunk_to_vbuf() does two
480-byte memcpy()s out of it.

A chunk that starts in the last 963 bytes of a packet therefore reads past
the data the device delivered, and for the final packet past the end of the
kcalloc(USBTV_ISOC_PACKETS, iso_size) transfer buffer. The bytes are copied
straight into the vb2 plane, so adjacent kernel heap is handed to whoever is
dequeuing V4L2 buffers.

Real hardware pads chunks to a 1024-byte stride, so the intermediate 256-byte
positions fail USBTV_MAGIC_OK() and the bug stays dormant; a malicious device
controls every payload byte and simply places the 0x88 magic at a tail offset.

Require a whole chunk to fit in the received data before scanning a position.
Every position at which a compliant device places a chunk is still visited.

  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in usbtv_iso_cb (drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:390 drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:435 drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:492)
  Read of size 480 at addr ffff88802d529e5c by task vhci_rx/5017

  Call Trace:
   __asan_memcpy (mm/kasan/shadow.c:105)
   usbtv_iso_cb (drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:390 drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:435 drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:492)
   __usb_hcd_giveback_urb (drivers/usb/core/hcd.c:1657)
   usb_hcd_giveback_urb (drivers/usb/core/hcd.c:1741)
   vhci_rx_loop (drivers/usb/usbip/vhci_rx.c:107 drivers/usb/usbip/vhci_rx.c:242)
   kthread (kernel/kthread.c:436)

  Allocated by task 5013:
   __kmalloc_noprof (mm/slub.c:5439)
   usbtv_start_streaming (drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:517 drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:586 drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c:771)
   vb2_start_streaming (drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c:1783)
   vb2_core_streamon (drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c:2336)
   vb2_ioctl_streamon (drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-v4l2.c:1105)

  The buggy address is located 7772 bytes inside of
  allocated 8000-byte region [ffff88802d528000, ffff88802d529f40)

Fixes: f3d27f34fdd7 ("[media] usbtv: Add driver for Fushicai USBTV007 video frame grabber")
Reported-by: Weiming Shi <bestswngs@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Xiang Mei <xmei5@asu.edu>
---
--- a/drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv.h
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv.h
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@
 
 #define USBTV_CHUNK_SIZE	256
 #define USBTV_CHUNK		240
+/* Bytes a chunk occupies: the header word plus USBTV_CHUNK data words. */
+#define USBTV_CHUNK_BYTES	(sizeof(__be32) * (USBTV_CHUNK + 1))
 
 #define USBTV_AUDIO_URBSIZE	20480
 #define USBTV_AUDIO_HDRSIZE	4
--- a/drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/usbtv/usbtv-video.c
@@ -483,12 +483,14 @@
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ip->number_of_packets; i++) {
-		int size = ip->iso_frame_desc[i].actual_length;
+		unsigned int size = ip->iso_frame_desc[i].actual_length;
 		unsigned char *data = ip->transfer_buffer +
 				ip->iso_frame_desc[i].offset;
 		int offset;
 
-		for (offset = 0; USBTV_CHUNK_SIZE * offset < size; offset++)
+		for (offset = 0;
+		     USBTV_CHUNK_SIZE * offset + USBTV_CHUNK_BYTES <= size;
+		     offset++)
 			usbtv_image_chunk(usbtv,
 				(__be32 *)&data[USBTV_CHUNK_SIZE * offset]);
 	}
